<header>
    <div class="button">Blind Cook Assistant</div>
</header>
<main>
    <h1>Welcome to Blind Cook Assistant</h1>
    
    <p>This web app allows you to generate recipe cards from YouTube videos and download them</p>
    <p>It's intended only for mobile</p>
    <p>First install the app as a Progressive Web App (PWA) by clicking the install button in your browser's address bar.</p>
    <p>Then go to any YouTube video(even shorts!) in the YouTube app</p>
    <p>Click share.</p>
    <p>Click more.</p>
    <p>Click Blind Cook</p>
    <p>Then you will be taken to a generation menu</p>
    <p>Click generate and wait for the recipe card to be generated</p>
    <p>After it's generated you can go to home and view your recipe cards.</p>
    <p>From there download the text or braille version of the recipe card</p></p>
    <p>Enjoy cooking with Blind Cook Assistant!</p>
    <h1>To return to this screen go to settings inside the app!</h1>
</main>
<footer>
    <a type="button" class="button" id="home" aria-label="Go home" href="/home">Home<a>
</footer>
<style>
    header,footer{
        grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }
    main{
        overflow-y:auto;
    }
</style>